WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.560
Hey Wisecrack, Jared here.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.480
Unless you’re living in a galaxy far, far
away, you’ve probably heard about the recent

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.790
Stars Wars backlash.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:20.090
Some fans hated The Last Jedi so much, they
issued an anti-Disney manifesto, run an actress

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:25.080
actress off instagram, are crowdfunding for a remake,
and have claimed credit for Solo’s failure

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.540
at the box office.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.650
There were even rumors that Kathleen Kennedy,
the president of Lucasfilms, would retire

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.670
early, possibly influenced by Twitter.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:37.910
This may seem like a bunch of fanboys throwing
tantrums or Russian bots, and while both of

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.080
those may be partly true, I can’t help but
think there’s something way deeper going

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.080
on, here.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.979
So, join us as we try to use philosophy to
explain the current crisis in the Star Wars

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:48.120
Universe.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:01:03.530
And some minor Last Jedi spoilers ahead.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.100
But first, a quick recap of what people hate
about the new Star Wars.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.570
While there’s some rather unpleasant threads
of criticism on the internet, some people

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:15.800
hate the new Star Wars for a reason that director
Rian Johnson is pretty overt about: subverting

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.930
the canon, or as he likes to call it - killing
the past.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:27.660
"A lot of times, I would say to Rian, we gotta
think about the fans, and he said, 'No, we

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:35.130
gotta think about the story, and we gotta
think about our movie,' which I, ya know uhh..."

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:40.230
Rey’s parents aren’t Skywalkers or Kenobis
or some other great family, but nobodies,

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:43.780
despite the constant mystery box teasing in
The Force Awakens.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:48.440
We get no storied rise of Snoke, or reveal
that he’s Mace Windu or something, just

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.690
an unceremonious death.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.110
And then, there’s Luke.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:56.280
We’re supposed to believe this wholesome
hero who once saw the light in the darkest

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.741
of villains is now throwing lightsabers off
cliffs and almost killing his child nephew?

00:02:00.741 --> 00:02:03.230
That just didn’t seem right.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:07.909
With Disney now putting all of their extended
universe movies on hold, and new Star Wars

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:13.670
spinoffs getting universally panned by fans,
it seems like the world of Star Wars in in

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.670
crisis.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:18.591
What’s happening with Star Wars is not so
different from a problem often faced by social

00:02:18.591 --> 00:02:23.660
systems or what political philosopher Jurgen
Habermas calls a legitimation crisis, i.e.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.150
an existential crisis that threatens the foundation
of a social system.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:32.370
Social systems are made up of three sub-parts:
the governmental, the socio-cultural, and

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.540
the economic.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.170
They all interact, and in some ways, these
three systems map onto the system of Star

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.180
Wars fandom.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.840
Let’s start with the government side.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:45.510
See, the system needs some kind of story or
idea to give it legitimacy.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.400
Governments do this through different means:
monarchies claim their legitimacy is derived

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.230
from God, democracies through election by
the people, constitutional governments through,

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.630
well, constitutions.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:03:00.040
Even dictators claim legitimacy in one way
or another, some by claiming they represent

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.530
the will of the people.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:07.090
Other things help too - making sure your citizens
are warm and fed, or the economic, does wonders

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:11.750
to make them ask fewer questions about how
or why you’re allowed to be in power.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:15.370
So, what happens when this is called into
question?

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:19.100
What happens when the people no longer feel
a system is upholding its values?

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.070
Or that those values are antiquated and useless?

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:26.630
What if people feel betrayed when a huge corporation
takes over their beloved franchise only to

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:30.650
birth what some consider to be an unholy abomination.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.230
When this happens, people stop obeying and
start rebelling.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:38.430
Think about countries whose populations take
to the streets when they suspect the new leaders

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:41.770
rigged the election, and therefore aren’t
legitimate.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:46.280
If we use this as a metaphor for Star Wars,
a lot of things start to make sense.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.910
Lucas was basically the divinely ordained
monarch of the Star Wars universe, which consisted

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:55.440
not just of the six films he made, but also
a ton of spin offs in the form of video games,

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:00.890
board games, cartoons, and tie-in novels that
got the Royal seal of approval from Lucasfilm.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.740
So, maybe it’s more like a constitutional
monarchy.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:07.769
But his legitimacy also came from the fact
that he, you know, created it all.

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:12.760
Together with Lucas, Star Wars fans helped
create a fully functioning social system,

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:17.190
with shared practices, beliefs, values, and
agreed upon rules of operation - that’s

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.930
what Habermas might call the socio-cultural
side of this system.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:26.360
Habermas calls this kind of socially cohesive
system lebenswelt, a lifeworld.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.490
And the Jedi could lebenswelt with the best
of them: the general meaning of Star Wars,

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:34.849
the values it represents, the characters it
has developed, the stories it tells, and the

00:04:34.849 --> 00:04:39.379
themes that define it were originally laid
out by Lucas and were more or less agreed

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.879
upon within the community.

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:43.889
Okay, maybe you hated Jar Jar, but you got
over it.

00:04:43.889 --> 00:04:47.879
Lucas’s word is still Star Wars law, even
if you don’t exactly like it.

00:04:47.879 --> 00:04:49.620
"I need a midichlorian count."

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:54.610
Like all lifeworlds, this Star Wars universe
also helped create a sense of individual identity

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:58.900
when people used these values and beliefs
to make meaning of their lives.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.949
That is, until 2012, when Disney bought Lucasfilms,
and shit started to get crazy.

00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:08.190
I guess you could say there's been a regime
change, and suddenly, at least from the perspective

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:12.869
of some fans, Lord Lucas was replaced by a
money-hungry animated mouse.

00:05:12.869 --> 00:05:15.580
"Now, do we have a problem?

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:16.580
Haha."

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:20.020
It’s the governmental equivalent of Queen
Elizabeth relinquishing the throne and, after

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:23.810
a nice bribe, handing the British Monarchy
to Mary Berry.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:27.809
After Disney gained rights to all Star Wars
intellectual property, and started making

00:05:27.809 --> 00:05:32.550
controversial decisions, they found themselves
in a big ol’ legitimation crisis.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:36.889
What the fanbase is going through can perhaps
be best understood by looking at one of the

00:05:36.889 --> 00:05:41.139
biggest legitimation crises of the last millenia
— one that changes the landscape of the

00:05:41.139 --> 00:05:42.139
entire world.

00:05:42.139 --> 00:05:46.999
You see, Disney is facing the same kind of
legitimation crisis the Catholic Church did

00:05:46.999 --> 00:05:50.809
in the 1500s, when their congregations began
to rebel.

00:05:50.809 --> 00:05:54.979
Up until the 16th century, the leadership
of the Catholic Church had total control over

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:59.350
the meaning of the Bible, since only priests,
bishops, the pope — and maybe the occasional

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:01.520
rich guy — had access to hard copies.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:07.069
Books, including the Bible, were so expensive
that very few ever learned to read.

00:06:07.069 --> 00:06:11.430
This famously allowed the Church to get away
with some seriously shady shit, like making

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:16.250
people pay the church in the form of indulgences
to get their loved ones out of purgatory.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:21.279
But all that changed when good ol’ Johnny
Gutenberg invented the printing press in 1440,

00:06:21.279 --> 00:06:23.870
and enabled the rapid reproduction of texts.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:28.189
Suddenly, regular people could read the Bible,
and what do you know, they had slightly different

00:06:28.189 --> 00:06:30.810
interpretations of some of those crucial texts.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:35.529
In this case, a crisis of legitimation happened
because the masses were no longer merely consuming

00:06:35.529 --> 00:06:39.860
religious meaning, but also helping produce
canonical interpretations.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:43.389
The legitimacy and authority of the Catholic
Church was seriously thrown into question

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:48.319
by people like Martin Luther, who posted 95
reasons why the Catholic Church sucked right

00:06:48.319 --> 00:06:49.520
on their front door.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.979
This crisis of legitimation, and the proliferation
of different kinds of christianity, really

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:58.590
sucked for Europe, as competing factions really,
really liked murdering each other.

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:02.310
So, in this metaphor, the bible is the original
Star Wars universe.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:05.429
And why did George Lucas get to interpret
it however he wanted?

00:07:05.429 --> 00:07:06.810
Because he wrote it.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:11.030
Maybe he’s not Jesus in this analogy, but
he’s at least an apostle or a prophet.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:16.330
But now the authority has moved from a single,
divinely inspired leader to a larger and fallible

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:21.360
organization, and people question why they
wield authority in developing quasi-holy texts

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.550
or its canon.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:26.569
In the recent films, but especially with the
Last Jedi, they changed many of the agreed

00:07:26.569 --> 00:07:29.830
upon values, meanings, and truths of the Star
Wars system.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:35.139
If there was just a change of hands from Lucas
to Disney, with the “administration” of

00:07:35.139 --> 00:07:38.759
Star Wars remaining mostly the same, people
may not have asked questions.

00:07:38.759 --> 00:07:43.060
But without the legitimacy of Lucas, people
started asking more questions.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.619
And Disney didn’t stop there.

00:07:44.619 --> 00:07:48.520
They also fucked with the very identity of
the community when they took a superlaser

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:53.470
to the cannon, decanonizing radio dramas,
video games, comics, and hundreds of spin-off

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:57.259
novels that Lucasfilm previously considered
part of the gospel.

00:07:57.259 --> 00:08:01.349
Remember that a lifeworld is important because
it defines a community by clarifying who’s

00:08:01.349 --> 00:08:03.370
in and out and who you can trust.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:07.499
You can’t just go around hacking and slashing
what counts as Star Wars, because people’s

00:08:07.499 --> 00:08:09.560
identities are wrapped up in this sh*t!

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:13.639
Star Wars enthusiasts aren’t just consumers
of this cannon, they’ve helped make the

00:08:13.639 --> 00:08:16.139
meaning of the Star Wars universe.

00:08:16.139 --> 00:08:20.259
Like the Catholic Church, Disney now faces
the wrath of the educated masses.

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:24.699
Except now, the problem isn’t just that
people can read: they blog, tweet, make video

00:08:24.699 --> 00:08:29.370
essays, produce their own cartoons, and stream
content to millions of viewers.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:33.720
And for every Martin Luther, there are a million
angry youtubers and vloggers, each posting

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:36.729
their own 95 problems with Disney Star Wars.

00:08:36.729 --> 00:08:41.630
We live in an age where people aren’t just
consuming media, but are also producing it.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.209
We’re prosumers.

00:08:43.209 --> 00:08:47.400
And if protestantism emerged with the printing
press and literacy took the interpretive power

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:52.120
away from the dudes with the funny hats, it
seems like the age of the prosumer empowers

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:56.100
people to criticize the few anointed successors
of Lucas.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:59.240
Now, prosumer: I know it sounds like we made
that word up.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:03.510
But it’s actually a technical term coined
in the 1980s by futurists Alvin and Heidi

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:08.930
Toffler to describe how the role of the producer
and consumer merge in the age of modern technology.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:12.840
Stars Wars fans are basically prosumers extraordinaire.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:18.160
Everyday fans have played a huge role in creating
meaning of Star Wars by sharing YouTube videos,

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:23.870
posting video essays or fan theories, subscribing
to /r/empiredidnothingwrong, or retweeting

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:24.870
LordPalpatine.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:30.180
In the age of prosumerism, every theory about
where Luke was all this time, who Snoke is,

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:34.870
which Jedi uses which lightsaber fighting
styles, is one way of contributing to the

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:35.870
Star Wars universe.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:39.430
It’s a way for the community to “practice”
Star Wars.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:43.260
Now imagine if you engage in your religious
tradition in your community, and all the sudden

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:47.280
the recently appointed church authority tells
you “YOU’RE DOING IT ALL WRONG!

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:49.220
THE WAFERS ARE A LIE!”

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:53.510
And while Star Wars may be the latest, it
isn’t the only franchise open to legitimation

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.410
crises within their communities.

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:59.840
Prosumerism is beginning to affect the relations
between fans and producers, even scaring away

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:04.470
James Mangold, director of Logan, who recently
tweeted: “At the point when work writing

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:08.370
&amp; directing big franchises has become the
emotionally loaded equivalent of writing a

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:13.320
new chapter of The Bible (w/ the probable
danger of being stoned &amp; called a blasphemer),

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:17.630
then a lot of bolder minds r gonna leave these
films 2 hacks &amp; corp boards."

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:22.080
So, is Star Wars system about to collapse
under the weight of its crisis?

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.080
Not necessarily.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:27.070
The Catholic Church obviously didn’t crumble
under their legitimation hiccup, and maybe

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:28.950
Star Wars won’t either.

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:31.210
Because the thing is, systems learn.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:35.090
After a few Vatican councils and papal deaths,
the Catholic Church managed to revise some

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:39.930
of the violent theology and resolidify the
community under common goals and shared beliefs.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:44.630
Sure, there were protestants who totally peaced
out and started their own thing, but in general,

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:47.400
the system learned, adjusted, and stayed in
tact.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:50.900
So, the question is, which direction will
the Star Wars system take?

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:55.510
Will Disney find a way to evolve in the time
of prosumerism, respecting their fans and

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.390
the universe they’ve helped create?

00:10:57.390 --> 00:11:01.270
Will fans choose to grow with the system,
and find new ways of interacting with their

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:02.610
beloved material?

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:06.980
Or will there be a reckoning, where Disney
and the fans part ways, like the Catholics

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:10.880
and Protestants, each starting their own version
of the religion and competing for the souls

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:11.920
of viewers?

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.240
Let us know what you guys think,

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.380
and if you enjoyed our take on the Star Wars crisis,

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.260
then I highly recommend checking out our friends over at Cheddar.

